caramos-ota (1.3.4-0caramos1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Release CaramOS 1.3.4.
  * Run all pending timestamp migrations by migration ID ledger.
  * New migration 20261105120000_keep_lotus_settings (tickets H-1092,
    H-1093, H-1104): the Lotus login helper copied the CaramOS defaults
    over ~/.config/fcitx5/profile and conf/lotus.conf whenever they
    differed from /etc/skel, so VNI, the Lotus mode, spell checking and
    shortcuts went back to the defaults at every login. It now only adds a
    default that is missing. The profile listed Lotus first, and Fcitx
    treats the first input method of a group as the "off" one, so every
    session started in English ("A"): the CaramOS profile now lists
    keyboard-us first with DefaultIM=lotus, and every session starts in
    Vietnamese ("V"); Ctrl+Shift still switches. Profiles someone changed
    stay as they are. Fcitx is stopped while its profile is rewritten, as
    it saves its own copy when it exits, and started again in the
    sessions of logged-in users.
  * New migration 20261105120100_search_menu_while_composing (ticket
    H-1098): the Start Menu search found nothing while Lotus was still
    composing a word (Preedit mode), only after a space. Cinnamenu now
    searches the text with the word being composed, and again as it
    changes, and is reloaded in running sessions. Hook 0170 takes
    Cinnamenu from the spices repository as it is when the ISO is built,
    so the patch knows both forms: 5.4.14 (the CaramOS 1.3.0 to 1.3.3
    ISOs) and 5.7 (ISOs built after 2026-10-30).
  * New migration 20261105120200_start_menu_file_search_without_freeze:
    the Start Menu's home folder search froze the desktop. It runs on
    Cinnamon's main loop and, for the files it found, waited for the disk
    (Cinnamenu 5.4.14 read the start of every file without a known
    extension, with blocking calls); it also went down into network
    drives mounted in the home folder (Google Drive with rclone). On a
    slow disk with a cold cache Cinnamon stalled 4.9 s (11 s with 5.7),
    and 17 s in all with a network drive. The search now takes a file's
    type from its name and stays on the file system of the home folder,
    out of other disks and network drives mounted in it: the longest
    stall is under half a second.
  * Update Center (tickets H-1102, H-1105): a software source added by
    another program that no longer works (an "https://github.io ./" line
    from an online guide) failed apt-get update, so the CaramOS update
    stopped. The CaramOS PPA is then updated alone and the update goes
    on, with the skipped source and its file in the OTA log.
  * Update Center (ticket H-1100): a package dpkg could not finish (Lotus
    3.5.6 on CaramOS 1.0.12, whose postinst has a syntax error, or an
    NVIDIA driver whose module does not build) failed every apt-get
    install, also the OTA self-update, though caramos-ota got installed.
    The self-update now counts as done when caramos-ota is at the new
    version, and names the broken packages; a broken Lotus is upgraded
    along with caramos-ota. apt-cache policy runs in English for this:
    on a Vietnamese system it says "Ứng cử:", not "Candidate:".
  * Update Center: what the OTA engine printed before it restarts itself
    after a self-update reaches the Update Center; Python's buffer was
    lost at execv when the output went to a pipe.
  * Driver Check (ticket H-1094): Ubuntu recommends NVIDIA 470 for Maxwell
    and Pascal cards (GeForce 940MX, GTX 1060), but 470 has no modules for
    Linux 6.14 and later and its DKMS build fails, which left dpkg broken.
    Only drivers with prebuilt signed modules are offered; a broken
    NVIDIA install is shown as a critical problem with the
    replacement driver; and the helper also installs the kernel those
    modules are built for, as the HWE modules follow the newest kernel.
  * Driver Check (tickets H-1085, H-1108, H-1109): a graphics driver turned
    off by nomodeset, <module>.modeset=0 or a blacklist says so, with the
    command or file that turns it on again.
  * Feedback & Help: system.log also carries the boot options, the
    packages dpkg did not finish, how the computer starts (BIOS or UEFI,
    Secure Boot, the UEFI entries of operating systems with the partition
    and file each starts) and its disks and partitions, for a grub> prompt
    (ticket H-1097). Firewall notices are left out, and a line the journal
    repeats comes once with a count, so the 200 lines keep the rest.
  * ISO: hook 0150 writes the new profile order and login helper, so the
    live USB and new installs start in Vietnamese too. The ISO build stops
    when the Cinnamenu it downloads lacks the Start Menu fixes.

