caramos-ota (1.3.3-0caramos1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Release CaramOS 1.3.3.
  * Run all pending timestamp migrations by migration ID ledger.
  * New migration 20261022120000_start_fcitx_at_login: Vietnamese typing
    works at every login again. org.fcitx.Fcitx5.desktop and the CaramOS
    Lotus login helper both declare X-GNOME-Provides=inputmethod, and
    Cinnamon's session runs only the one it reads first: always the helper
    on the live USB, and on about half of new installs. Since migration
    20261010120100 the helper only restarted Fcitx when a default differed
    from /etc/skel, so in every live session and at every login of those
    new installs nothing started Fcitx, and Telex typing gave letters
    without accents. The helper now also starts Fcitx when it is not
    running, and the migration starts it at once in the sessions of people
    logged in during the update.

