caramos-ota (1.3.0-0caramos1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Release CaramOS 1.3.0.
  * Run all pending timestamp migrations by migration ID ledger.
  * Install the App Center (caramos-app-center, the app picker) from its
    GitHub releases and keep it up to date in the daily check. Releases are
    verified against the App Center release key shipped in
    /usr/share/caramos-ota/keys before anything is installed.
  * Put an App Center launcher on each user's Desktop and in /etc/skel.
  * Update Center: redesign in the Vietnam Linux Family colours; the page
    scrolls above a fixed button bar, so "Update now" stays visible on small
    screens (#77). Pin Gdk 3.0 so it still opens next to the GTK 4 App Center,
    show its taskbar icon, and translate the password prompt.
  * Installer slideshow: Zalo is preselected in the App Center instead of
    preinstalled.
  * Stop shipping __pycache__ bytecode written by tests and manifest checks.
  * Lighten the desktop session: about 150 MiB less RAM five minutes after an
    automatic login on the test VMs, 50 MiB below Linux Mint 22.3. Fill GTK
    3's OpenGL visual cache before the session daemons start, keep Fcitx 5
    from starting the XDG portals, start Flameshot without OpenGL, start the
    calendar reminder daemon (and with it the Evolution data server) once
    there is an event, a task or a calendar account, hide the print queue
    applet, and disable cups-browsed and kerneloops.
  * Recommend and configure earlyoom: when RAM and swap are nearly full it
    stops the app using the most memory instead of letting the machine
    freeze while it swaps. It never picks the session's own processes.
  * Boot no longer reloads systemd for the Lotus input method; login no
    longer restarts Fcitx when its settings did not change, nor resets the
    Flameshot shortcut.
  * Control Center: query VPN connections while the menu is open instead of
    running nmcli twice every 15 seconds.
  * System Reports tray: look for running Timeshift snapshots and automatic
    updates once a minute instead of every 10 seconds; each check read the
    command line of every process.
  * Remove the 14 Tela icon colours CaramOS does not use (about 1.1 GiB).
  * Add Driver Check (caramos-driver-check, in the menu): see which hardware
    works and which drivers are missing (Wi-Fi, wired network, graphics,
    sound, Bluetooth, webcam, fingerprint reader), with each fix explained.
    It installs the NVIDIA and Broadcom Wi-Fi drivers Ubuntu recommends with
    one click, opens at the first login and in the live session, and then
    only speaks up about new problems.
  * Add Feedback & Help: a question mark at the right end of the panel and
    the caramos-help window, to ask Vietnam Linux Family for help, report a
    bug or send feedback, with the hw-probe hardware profile and the Driver
    Check results when the user ticks them.
  * Requests can carry up to five screenshots, screen recordings, pictures
    or videos (up to a minute each), made smaller and without location data.
  * Requests are shared with the VNLF community unless the user unticks it:
    a moderator reviews them before they are public; the contact never is.
  * The panel menu lists the last requests with VNLF's status and the
    community's answers, and the window lists all of them; a notification
    tells when VNLF or the community answers.
  * Stop CopyQ from starting at login; it stays installed with its history,
    and new installs no longer include it.

